NXR-145|Explicit boot-stack RAM budget|Memory|The RISCue build shall expose a validated boot-stack reserve and derive the footprint reserve from final linker symbols.|Reduce conservative RAM reservations transparently without claiming unqualified stack safety.|Default remains 4096 bytes; reject malformed, unaligned or out-of-range settings and image overlap; footprint rejects missing symbols and counts the actual reserve; document startup and first-trap call-chain analysis.|Default and reduced-reserve cross-links, invalid configuration rejection, footprint comparison and later board stack qualification.|NXR-142|RTOS_BOOT_STACK_BYTES decimal 512..32512 aligned 16; default 4096.|No new runtime storage; reserved boot stack is explicit and separate from thread stacks.|cmake/configuration.cmake,cmake/firmware.cmake,ports/riscue/link.ld,tools/NexRT.Workbench/Program.cs,docs/memory.rst|Configuration and linker symbols expose the reservation; reducing it remains subject to application and hardware stack qualification.|cmake/configuration.cmake,cmake/firmware.cmake,ports/riscue/link.ld,tools/NexRT.Workbench/Program.cs||PartialSourceUnverified
NXR-146|Ground-linked diagnostic packages|Diagnostics|The optional diagnostic service shall accept ground-linked flat images for a boot-reserved execution slot without target ELF parsing or symbol resolution.|Upload small diagnostics or a shell while retaining ELF and debug symbols on the ground.|Ground tool uses exact firmware ID, ISA, ABI and slot address; rejects unresolved relocations and unsupported runtime features; manifest bounds entry, initialized data and BSS; moving the slot requires relinking or ground relocation.|Future native C# packager checks, malformed package cases, exact-slot linking and qualified target execution.|NXR-144|Optional default-off service; fixed address and capacity; native C# XDoc ground tooling.|Fixed slot includes code/constants/data/BSS; no heap or runtime thread registration.|docs/diagnostic-overlays.rst,docs/memory.rst,ports/riscue/start.S|Only the design is present; no packager, transfer receiver or executable publication hook is implemented.
NXR-147|Diagnostic activation and ownership|Diagnostics|The diagnostic worker shall validate and publish uploaded code only while the reserved slot is quiescent and board execution coherency is established.|Prevent partial images and stale callbacks from executing while preserving static storage.|Precreated worker and scratch capacity; bounded authenticated transfer according to mission policy; digest alone is not authentication; no retained overlay callbacks; explicit states; cache publication hook required; failed transfers stay inactive; hung-code recovery uses qualified watchdog/reset.|Future transfer state-machine and stale-reference checks, cache publication review and hardware fault recovery exercises.|NXR-146|One optional permanent worker and slot; default off; no forced concurrent unload.|Fixed worker stack/control, bounded receiver state/buffer; avoid a second full image buffer.|docs/diagnostic-overlays.rst,include/rtos.hpp,ports/riscue/rtos_port.hpp|Design only; current machine-mode execution has no isolation and software deadlines cannot contain a hung privileged diagnostic.
NXR-148|Board-qualified QSPI boot and XIP|Boot|A QSPI boot target shall distinguish flash storage with RAM copy from memory-mapped execute-in-place and declare its actual startup and flash-busy contract.|Use nonvolatile storage without overstating RAM savings or assuming SPI implies instruction fetch support.|Verify reset path, instruction-fetch mapping, flash mode, cache/latency and erase/program behavior; XIP linker separates load and execution addresses and startup copies writable data; code required during flash busy resides in safe memory; publish measured RAM only after cross-link and board validation.|Future board memory-map review, boot/data-copy execution, flash-busy interrupt exercises and measured footprint.|NXR-144|Board-specific optional boot/XIP adapter; existing flat RAM remains supported.|Writable data and stacks remain in RAM; account bootstrap, RAM handlers and controller buffers explicitly.|docs/diagnostic-overlays.rst,ports/riscue/link.ld,ports/riscue/start.S|Planned only; no verified QSPI controller, executable flash address, XIP linker or data-copy startup is available.
